        "id": "U10-D2",
        "statement": "A copy set aside is part of the hold. Tier 1 Hold has a new field, SetAside: SetAside option, where SetAside = { Copy; Until }. None means the member is still waiting. So a set-aside copy always belongs to exactly one hold and has exactly one deadline, and removing the hold (on borrowing or expiry) frees the copy without any extra step. In JSON, \u0027setAside\u0027 is written only when present. Holds stored before L10 have no \u0027setAside\u0027 and load as waiting.",
